//! Electronic tubes (manual 4.9): each a node shape, and its variants by its options
//! (`filament`, `nocathode`, `fullcathode`, `nixieanode`…, `anodes`), named `diodetube|filament`.
//! Each is measured too with each of its sizes changed (`triode@width`, `@filament_angle`…) and
//! the pairs of them that change it together, drawn in between; a tube wider than tall
//! (`tubes/width` over `tubes/height`) has rounder ends, and its own measures (`triode~wide`).
//!
//! Measured on what CircuiTikZ 1.8.7 draws (`tools/oracle/`), at the default size, in
//! `bipoles/length`; the text goes right of the `text` anchor (in the middle of a magnetron) and
//! does not count in the picture's size.

// measured numbers, some of which happen to be close to constants like 2/π
#![allow(clippy::approx_constant)]

